WEBVTT

00:12.554 --> 00:14.305
I'm uh... gonna go buy a drink.

00:14.389 --> 00:15.473
Wait, Amamiya.

00:15.557 --> 00:16.683
I'm coming too.

00:24.816 --> 00:25.984
Without a word...

00:26.568 --> 00:27.902
We've arrived...

00:36.911 --> 00:38.163
[REACTION}

00:38.705 --> 00:39.581
Hey, hey,

00:39.664 --> 00:43.084
When they come back to the classroom
from getting their drinks, what do you

00:43.168 --> 00:45.295
think they'd do if we suddenly
weren't here?

00:45.378 --> 00:47.505
THE TWO HAVE COMPLETELY LOST FOCUS

00:47.589 --> 00:48.423
Should we?

00:50.425 --> 00:51.384
THUMP, THUMP, THUMP

00:51.468 --> 00:52.302
So hot.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.095
- Minato!
- So cold.

00:54.179 --> 00:55.764
Mm? Oh.

00:55.847 --> 00:57.390
Hey, how's it going Kenta!

00:57.474 --> 00:59.434
You studying the past exams I gave you?

01:01.269 --> 01:02.228
It's a senior.

01:03.271 --> 01:05.440
- Scurry, scurry, scurry.
- I was studying them, but I just

01:05.523 --> 01:07.400
- took a break.
- Is that really true?

01:08.777 --> 01:10.820
- An underclassman?
- Yeah. Ain't he cute?

01:11.321 --> 01:13.198
Is Kenta being a good senior to you?

01:13.698 --> 01:17.160
He's always acting like he's hot
stuff, but he's mostly just trouble.

01:17.243 --> 01:19.329
- Fade...
- What're you saying?

01:20.538 --> 01:22.207
- See ya.
- Later.

01:22.290 --> 01:23.708
- Bye.
- Later!

01:24.209 --> 01:25.627
Are you done talking?

01:25.710 --> 01:26.753
HIkawa.

01:27.504 --> 01:30.507
You know you didn't have to lie low just
because of them.

01:30.590 --> 01:33.635
Oh, it's more like I was kinda
just hiding because they were

01:33.718 --> 01:35.345
upperclassmen I didn't know.

01:35.845 --> 01:37.430
Were you afraid?

01:38.264 --> 01:39.682
MEMORIES OF JUNIOR HIGH

01:39.766 --> 01:40.683
- Kinda.
- Mmm.

01:40.767 --> 01:42.102
Shy around new people.

01:42.727 --> 01:43.561
Oh.

01:48.650 --> 01:50.527
- Hey, Hikawa
- Uh-huh?

01:51.027 --> 01:53.863
Then are you afraid of me?

01:54.656 --> 01:55.490
Huh?

01:58.034 --> 01:59.828
- Mm-mm.
- Not anymore.

02:00.537 --> 02:01.496
No, absolutely not.

02:08.711 --> 02:10.547
Man, I'm so glad.

02:13.800 --> 02:16.177
- Huh?
- That's right.

02:16.678 --> 02:20.682
Amamiya's human just like me, and gets
hurt and worries about things, too

02:21.891 --> 02:23.893
I mean that should be obvious but...

02:25.562 --> 02:28.565
How had I been acting toward him
this whole time?

02:32.068 --> 02:32.902
Hey, Amamiya.

02:33.403 --> 02:34.445
What do I do?

02:34.529 --> 02:36.364
I can't look her in the eye.

02:37.824 --> 02:39.909
- [REACTION}
- [REACTION}

02:39.993 --> 02:40.994
Huh?

02:43.413 --> 02:44.247
Co-! Co-!

02:45.582 --> 02:47.625
- Co?
- Cockroach! There's a cockroach!

02:47.709 --> 02:48.835
- Whoa!
- Ah! See?!

02:49.961 --> 02:51.671
- There! There!
- Huh? Wait, what?

02:52.172 --> 02:53.006
Ugh!

02:55.216 --> 02:56.050
Uh...

02:56.926 --> 02:57.760
Uh...

02:58.678 --> 02:59.512
- Uh.
- Uh.

03:00.013 --> 03:00.847
GIGGLE

03:00.930 --> 03:01.806
CHUCKLE

03:03.766 --> 03:04.601
I can't!

03:07.020 --> 03:08.605
You were losing your mind!

03:08.688 --> 03:09.731
I was.

03:10.648 --> 03:11.482
Sorry.

03:12.942 --> 03:16.279
I don't wanna get close to her by forcing
my way through the door.

03:17.030 --> 03:19.866
I wanna do it the right way, and
be friends.

03:20.700 --> 03:21.743
And see her smile.

03:22.994 --> 03:23.828
That's all.

03:26.080 --> 03:27.540
That's all I want.

03:28.458 --> 03:29.459
And yet...

05:01.926 --> 05:05.722
Self-awareness

05:06.764 --> 05:08.516
Well, those two aren't coming back.

05:10.685 --> 05:13.479
Don't you think they're taking way
too long of a break? Do they even plan

05:13.563 --> 05:15.606
to study? We have exams!

05:15.690 --> 05:17.442
That doesn't sound like you at all.

05:18.151 --> 05:21.988
EXECUTING THE "WILL THEY BE SURPRISED
IF NO ONE'S HERE WHEN THEY COME BACK?"

05:23.823 --> 05:24.907
Do you like anyone?

05:26.951 --> 05:28.244
Wh- why do you wanna know?

05:28.328 --> 05:32.749
Well, I never hear stuff like that about
you, so I couldn't help but be curious.

05:38.796 --> 05:39.630
Miki.

05:46.888 --> 05:47.722
Koyun...

05:48.348 --> 05:49.182
Huh?

05:49.265 --> 05:51.184
Hayato, Daichi, and Gin.

05:51.684 --> 05:53.853
Dad, Mom, Haruto, Sakura...

05:54.354 --> 05:56.439
Wait, wait, wait. You're missing someone.

05:56.522 --> 05:58.191
Why aren't you mentioning Minato?

06:02.028 --> 06:03.196
Well, Yota.

06:03.696 --> 06:07.617
If you ever do find someone you like,
I just want you to know that you have my

06:07.700 --> 06:08.868
full support.

06:09.369 --> 06:11.913
After all, you've done so much for me.

06:17.835 --> 06:19.796
- You're such a good friend!
- Yay!

06:22.090 --> 06:23.132
Oh, they're back!

06:25.093 --> 06:26.344
Huh? They're gone.

06:26.427 --> 06:27.929
Their bags are still here.

06:28.012 --> 06:29.097
Bathroom break?

06:31.265 --> 06:33.142
Well, they'll be back eventually.

06:33.643 --> 06:34.977
I guess you're right.

06:38.314 --> 06:41.943
The way Yota hides his feelings for her,
while trying to stay friends with

06:42.026 --> 06:43.486
her and pretending it's fine...

06:44.070 --> 06:46.489
You can tell he's working hard
to shove it down.

06:47.365 --> 06:51.202
On that note, if Hikawa were to fall for
Yota, then her feelings wouldn't be

06:51.285 --> 06:52.912
reciprocated.

06:54.747 --> 06:56.040
She shouldn't go there.

06:57.250 --> 06:58.501
Or that's what I thought.

06:59.877 --> 07:01.421
But easier said than done.

07:01.504 --> 07:04.424
That's not something you can just turn on
and off at will.

07:06.008 --> 07:06.843
Ahhh...

07:07.593 --> 07:09.512
I wish I hadn't noticed.

07:10.555 --> 07:13.141
I feel like she finally opened her
heart up to me a little, but now...

07:13.224 --> 07:16.227
I have to be more careful moving forward.

07:16.310 --> 07:17.145
Amamiya.

07:20.982 --> 07:23.693
Here you go. I only had two of them left.

07:23.776 --> 07:25.194
So I want you to have one.

07:27.447 --> 07:29.198
Uh. Th-Thanks.

07:31.742 --> 07:33.703
Ahhh. I really hate this.

07:34.787 --> 07:37.123
You weren't gonna share the candy
with us, huh?

07:37.206 --> 07:38.040
You were there?

07:43.212 --> 07:45.506
ART ROOM

07:45.590 --> 07:48.134
Hey, Tsukiko, have you always eaten
in the art room?

07:48.217 --> 07:49.051
Yeah.

07:49.135 --> 07:50.261
This way I can eat quickly and
then continue working during

07:50.344 --> 07:51.179
my lunch break.

07:52.847 --> 07:55.057
- How practical.
- Remember me?

07:55.141 --> 07:56.225
From episode six!

07:56.309 --> 07:57.768
Tsukiko Shimojima.

07:58.561 --> 08:02.565
So towards the beginning, I started out
by eating with everyone in the classroom

08:03.065 --> 08:04.984
But our group was pretty big.

08:09.155 --> 08:13.075
But there was this kind of unspoken rule
that no one would start eating 'til

08:13.159 --> 08:15.369
everyone was there.

08:16.120 --> 08:18.498
I started to think, "Wait, hold on,
this isn't right."

08:18.581 --> 08:20.416
"This doesn't mean being close."

08:20.500 --> 08:24.170
Then I just started to slowly distance
myself, and broke away from them.

08:24.253 --> 08:25.546
HA HA...

08:26.047 --> 08:27.173
Ah!

08:27.840 --> 08:30.760
Oh, but just to be clear, I'm not on bad
terms with anyone.

08:30.843 --> 08:33.387
I hang out with them separately,
even now, and...

08:33.471 --> 08:37.225
Oh no! I just told her something that
reveals how terrible I am! Ahhh!

08:37.308 --> 08:38.768
- I get it.
- Huh?

08:38.851 --> 08:41.395
In fact I get it so much I feel sick.

08:42.063 --> 08:45.066
- Empathy.
- Um. A- Are you okay?

08:45.691 --> 08:48.945
You see, I'm not good in group settings
either.

08:49.529 --> 08:51.197
To be honest, I can totally tell.

08:54.450 --> 08:55.284
Hmm.

08:55.952 --> 08:56.953
Oh, man.

08:57.453 --> 09:00.831
You know, I really wish you and I had
started talking way sooner.

09:07.213 --> 09:08.047
- What?
- Oh!

09:08.130 --> 09:10.091
GRADE 1 CLASS 6 AFTER SCHOOL STUDY TIME

09:13.928 --> 09:15.179
Are you in the mood... Hey.

09:15.930 --> 09:17.098
For some curry?

09:17.682 --> 09:18.516
- Huh?
- Huh?

09:18.599 --> 09:20.393
- Huh?
- Do you ever not want curry?

09:20.476 --> 09:21.519
Come on.

09:21.602 --> 09:23.771
Oh. You're going along with this. Good.

09:24.272 --> 09:27.692
Apparently, there's a famous curry
place in the new mall that opened

09:34.031 --> 09:36.284
- I don't mind.
- Me neither.

09:36.367 --> 09:37.868
What about your family dinner?

09:38.369 --> 09:40.830
Koyun, you always seem to be
worried about that.

09:40.913 --> 09:41.872
It's alright.

09:41.956 --> 09:42.790
Uh, "Always?"

09:43.416 --> 09:45.459
Yes! Alright!

09:45.543 --> 09:46.669
Let's go!

09:47.295 --> 09:50.590
- Trot, trot, trot, trot, trot, trot, trot,
- Trot, trot, trot, trot, trot, trot, trot,

09:50.673 --> 09:51.507
Wow.

09:52.091 --> 09:54.176
Yota, you're able to hold onto that part?

09:54.260 --> 09:55.094
What?

09:55.177 --> 09:56.012
SPARKLE, SPARKLE

09:56.095 --> 09:57.513
- That's so nice.
- Is it?

09:57.597 --> 09:59.599
I can stand without holding anything.

10:00.266 --> 10:01.100
Core strength!

10:01.183 --> 10:02.685
Why's it a competition?

10:06.063 --> 10:08.149
- You're heavy.
- Hold yourself up!

10:08.774 --> 10:10.568
I'm not using my hands so it counts.

10:10.651 --> 10:11.736
That's so cheating.

10:25.708 --> 10:29.587
It wasn't all that long ago... that things
were so different.

10:32.923 --> 10:36.260
In junior high, it's like I was
living in a fish tank, despite not

10:36.344 --> 10:38.554
being able to breathe underwater.

10:39.805 --> 10:42.808
Being different from everyone else was
total agony for me.

10:43.851 --> 10:46.145
I decided it wasn't where I belonged.

10:47.104 --> 10:49.690
But then I found out I didn't belong
anywhere.

10:50.650 --> 10:53.527
I was ashamed I couldn't seem to
figure out how to adapt.

10:54.195 --> 10:55.029
It hurt.

10:55.529 --> 10:56.364
A lot.

10:57.698 --> 10:58.532
But...

11:00.368 --> 11:03.788
Once I was able to get out of the
fish tank, I realized that none of

11:03.871 --> 11:06.582
it actually had to be that painful.

11:07.375 --> 11:10.961
I just needed to break free from that
small world I had been living in.

11:12.046 --> 11:14.006
Everything just seemed so trivial then.

11:18.052 --> 11:20.930
Club activities, school events and even
friendships.

11:21.931 --> 11:25.393
If I could get through high school
in peace, I felt like nothing else

11:25.476 --> 11:26.435
mattered.

11:31.357 --> 11:33.275
The world around me has changed, but...

11:34.819 --> 11:35.653
Wow!

11:35.736 --> 11:38.739
The area around here has become so nice,
hasn't it?

11:38.823 --> 11:41.242
Can I say that I myself have really
changed?

11:42.785 --> 11:45.037
So much has changed since they
built the mall.

11:45.121 --> 11:47.331
I bet the rent around here has gone up
like crazy.

11:47.415 --> 11:48.290
Why do you care?

11:49.125 --> 11:51.127
Yeah. It'll be okay.

11:51.919 --> 11:53.462
Those bad memories...

11:54.046 --> 11:55.798
I can act like they never happened.

11:56.674 --> 12:00.678
GRAND OPENING SALE NOW IN PROGRESS

12:01.721 --> 12:02.555
Okay.

12:03.222 --> 12:06.642
We're right here and the food court
is here, so this way.

12:07.184 --> 12:08.310
POWER WALKING

12:08.394 --> 12:09.395
Gah! Uh!

12:11.731 --> 12:13.691
- Happen. It's the opposite direction.
- Hm?

12:13.774 --> 12:14.775
Here, this way.

12:15.484 --> 12:17.445
Really? This isn't a trick?

12:17.528 --> 12:18.612
I promise you.

12:19.447 --> 12:21.866
What was that whole, "I know you so well"
thing?

12:29.832 --> 12:30.666
- Hm?
- Seriously?

12:30.750 --> 12:31.584
Yep!

12:34.712 --> 12:35.546
Huh?

12:36.338 --> 12:38.090
- Miki!
- What?! What do you want?

12:38.591 --> 12:39.884
Igarashi is here.

12:42.344 --> 12:44.346
We're actually not on very good terms.

12:44.930 --> 12:47.600
He and Hikawa really shouldn't see each
other, right?

12:49.518 --> 12:51.020
I'm assuming Koyun told you?

12:51.854 --> 12:53.022
That they dated.

12:53.522 --> 12:54.482
Yeah...

12:54.565 --> 12:55.691
She told me a little.

12:56.192 --> 12:57.860
Like they're on bad terms.

12:58.402 --> 13:00.738
If they ran into each other, would they
fight?

13:01.447 --> 13:04.033
No, I don't think it would go that far,
but...

13:04.116 --> 13:07.620
Well, if it's going to upset Hikawa,
then we don't want them seeing

13:07.703 --> 13:08.621
each other.

13:09.163 --> 13:10.206
Mm-hm, agreed.

13:10.706 --> 13:11.540
Hm?

13:16.587 --> 13:17.630
What's wrong, Koyun?

13:18.714 --> 13:19.715
I can't let him see!

13:20.299 --> 13:22.009
- Yota, look! A dog over there! Let's go
- Huh?

13:22.092 --> 13:23.302
- See it!
- Uh, wait, what?

13:23.385 --> 13:25.805
I mean, who knows, maybe nothing will
happen either.

13:25.888 --> 13:28.974
It's possible he may have just moved
past it by now anyway.

13:29.683 --> 13:31.894
Oh... That's possible.

13:32.520 --> 13:33.395
Hikawa?

13:34.271 --> 13:37.024
No, there was no one by that name in our
junior high.

13:39.568 --> 13:42.947
But still, I don't know how you could
forget someone's existence.

13:43.697 --> 13:47.034
Well, there shouldn't be an issue if
things are going well with his new

13:47.117 --> 13:48.410
girlfriend, right?.

13:48.494 --> 13:49.537
Huh?

13:50.204 --> 13:51.455
Oh. Never mind.

13:51.539 --> 13:52.498
Thinking out loud here.

13:52.581 --> 13:56.043
I don't know anything about his love life
after starting high school.

13:56.836 --> 13:59.755
Maybe he doesn't even have one. But it
seems like he would, right? I have no

13:59.839 --> 14:01.215
- idea, though.
- Girlfriend?

14:02.591 --> 14:03.425
Huh?

14:05.803 --> 14:08.180
- Thank you for the meal.
- Thank you for the meal.

14:08.264 --> 14:10.850
- Hey, hey, hey! Get out of my way!
- So loud!

14:11.350 --> 14:12.726
PLAYER FOUR - PLAYER THREE

14:12.810 --> 14:13.644
Huh.

14:13.727 --> 14:17.147
- I'll be damned if I allow anybody to race
- Oh man, someone's using it right now.

14:17.231 --> 14:18.148
Ahead of me! Over my dead body,
you hear me?

14:18.232 --> 14:19.441
We'll go somewhere else.

14:20.067 --> 14:23.612
ONDO MASTER

14:23.696 --> 14:24.530
- Wah!
- Oh!

14:24.613 --> 14:27.992
UPPI PRINT STICKER

14:28.075 --> 14:29.326
Do it! Why can't you?

14:29.410 --> 14:32.413
- We're here, so we might as well just
- Uhhh, are you sure I can go in here?

14:32.496 --> 14:33.330
I get nervous.

14:33.414 --> 14:34.790
Let's go! Three, two, one!

14:34.874 --> 14:35.708
Yay!

14:37.293 --> 14:40.254
I ended up having a really good time in
spite of myself.

14:40.337 --> 14:42.548
Goofing off before exams feels
incredible.

14:43.048 --> 14:44.508
I could get used to this.

14:44.592 --> 14:46.176
Well, don't make a habit of it.

14:46.886 --> 14:48.470
We'll study some more tomorrow.

14:49.972 --> 14:50.806
Yota!

14:52.725 --> 14:53.601
See ya!

14:54.393 --> 14:55.561
- See you later.
- Later.

15:03.611 --> 15:04.445
Nicely done.

15:05.029 --> 15:05.863
Huh?

15:05.946 --> 15:06.780
For what?

15:09.867 --> 15:14.121
There shouldn't be an issue if things are
going well with his new girlfriend right?

15:14.204 --> 15:16.957
I mean of course she's had past romantic
relationships.

15:17.833 --> 15:20.085
But it still took me by surprise.

15:20.169 --> 15:21.587
And with Igarashi?

15:23.172 --> 15:27.092
I mean, when I look at it objectively,
it at least kind of makes sense how she

15:27.176 --> 15:29.219
might have feelings for Yota, but...

15:29.803 --> 15:31.555
No, don't think about that!

15:34.350 --> 15:35.601
Ohhh, man.

15:37.937 --> 15:39.813
I just don't get it.

15:44.360 --> 15:46.070
Yep, vators are the best!

15:46.904 --> 15:50.741
The only person who'd call an elevator a
"vator", would be you Mi- ki...

15:51.659 --> 15:52.493
Huh?

15:59.625 --> 16:00.876
In junior high...

16:02.294 --> 16:04.088
I hated Tsubasa Igarashi.

16:05.047 --> 16:08.175
- That doesn't look very interesting.
- Mismatched personalities.

16:08.258 --> 16:10.094
- A one-sided affection.
- I'm serious!

16:10.177 --> 16:11.804
Come on, you've got Igarashi, right?

16:11.887 --> 16:14.181
Even those on the sidelines involving
themselves in my life.

16:14.264 --> 16:15.432
Yuishira, don't keep Igarashi waiting too
long.

16:15.516 --> 16:16.850
I hated it.

16:16.934 --> 16:17.893
I hated everything.

16:19.687 --> 16:23.190
But none of that's why I've been avoiding
him or even discussing him.

16:24.692 --> 16:27.277
This is a problem within myself.

16:30.447 --> 16:31.407
Oh, it's you.

16:31.991 --> 16:32.825
Huh?

16:34.493 --> 16:35.744
What's with that hair?

16:36.495 --> 16:37.329
GASP

16:37.413 --> 16:38.872
What about my hair? Huh?

16:38.956 --> 16:41.417
It was pretty weird the last time I saw
you, too

16:41.500 --> 16:45.129
What? I- It doesn't matter either way.
I look good in anything, no matter

16:45.212 --> 16:49.091
MATCHING HIS ENERGY FOR THE TIME BEING
MATCHING HIS ENERGY FOR THE TIME BEING

16:49.174 --> 16:51.301
I'm being treated as if I'm not
even here.

16:52.469 --> 16:55.973
After jumping out of the fish tank, the
more I get to know myself, the

16:56.056 --> 16:57.933
more I hate it.

17:02.521 --> 17:03.355
I...

17:04.356 --> 17:07.568
I never, ever had any feelings for you.

17:08.485 --> 17:12.281
I avoided him because I was scared
to face the person I hurt so maliciously.

17:12.364 --> 17:13.574
That's all.

17:14.408 --> 17:15.701
I'm just a coward.

17:18.287 --> 17:19.121
Well, see ya.

17:24.543 --> 17:25.419
Igarashi!

17:31.008 --> 17:31.884
What do you want?

17:32.426 --> 17:33.260
Uh.

17:33.844 --> 17:36.096
Has high school... been fun?

17:38.015 --> 17:40.059
Huh? What are you?

17:40.142 --> 17:42.436
My weird old aunt or something?

17:42.519 --> 17:45.522
BONG

17:45.606 --> 17:46.440
Wait.

17:46.523 --> 17:47.357
What do I do?

17:47.441 --> 17:49.526
As expected the conversation
doesn't flow.

17:49.610 --> 17:50.694
It's going fine.

17:50.778 --> 17:51.612
Huh?

17:52.154 --> 17:54.656
I mean, not like I need your concern or
anything.

18:00.788 --> 18:06.001
You know, when you stopped Igarashi
back there, man, I was totally surprised.

18:06.585 --> 18:07.586
Oh, thank you.

18:08.796 --> 18:09.630
I dunno.

18:09.713 --> 18:12.800
Maybe it's because hanging out
with you guys was so much fun.

18:13.801 --> 18:17.096
That could be why I acted so outta the
norm.

18:17.763 --> 18:18.597
Koyun.

18:26.146 --> 18:27.815
Here, thanks for this.

18:28.524 --> 18:30.484
Huh? What's with the lame bag?

18:30.984 --> 18:32.444
What, who cares what it looks like?

18:32.528 --> 18:33.403
You're just going home.

18:33.487 --> 18:35.989
It's not like you're gonna meet anyone on
the way.

18:37.491 --> 18:38.575
But I did meet someone.

18:38.659 --> 18:40.119
And of all people...

18:40.661 --> 18:42.412
Has high school... been fun?

18:43.413 --> 18:44.873
That's rich coming from you.

18:47.626 --> 18:48.460
Pain in the ass.

18:52.756 --> 18:53.590
Hey, so...

18:54.341 --> 18:57.386
It's my fault that you dated Igarashi,
isn't it?

18:58.303 --> 18:59.138
Sorry.

18:59.221 --> 19:01.974
It's because I wasn't considerate of
your feelings and said things I

19:02.057 --> 19:02.891
should've have.

19:04.935 --> 19:07.062
- Huh?
- Huh?

19:07.604 --> 19:09.648
Huh? What shouldn't you have said?

19:09.731 --> 19:10.899
Hold on, wait.

19:10.983 --> 19:14.403
Don't you remember what I told you
when we chatted here awhile back.

19:14.486 --> 19:16.989
How you should be glad to be liked and
not be greedy?

19:17.072 --> 19:19.575
Now that you mention it, I guess
you might have.

19:19.658 --> 19:21.368
What?! Wait, that's it?

19:21.869 --> 19:24.204
Sorry to disappoint, my memory's
a bit fuzzy.

19:24.288 --> 19:25.372
CONFUSION

19:25.455 --> 19:27.916
What?!
Wait, then why did you date Igarashi?

19:28.417 --> 19:29.459
Hmm.

19:32.045 --> 19:33.213
- That's secret.
- What?!

19:33.297 --> 19:34.131
DEVASTATED

19:34.214 --> 19:36.550
Because if I told you, you'd think
less of me.

19:38.552 --> 19:39.386
Wait a minute.

19:40.012 --> 19:40.846
Huh?

19:41.471 --> 19:43.974
- I'm not just gonna let that
- I'm not just gonna let that comment

19:44.057 --> 19:45.309
- comment slide.
- slide.

19:46.602 --> 19:47.436
Well, I...

19:48.896 --> 19:52.482
I thought I'd feel better about myself if
maybe I could fall for someone...

19:52.566 --> 19:54.151
Someone who loves me back.

19:55.444 --> 19:58.697
But instead of feeling better, I was just
in pain the whole time.

19:59.489 --> 20:01.283
And I ended up hurting Igarashi.

20:02.868 --> 20:04.912
Or I went out of my way to.

20:06.413 --> 20:08.498
My actions weren't lining up with my
heart.

20:08.582 --> 20:10.792
And I was really only thinking of myself.

20:11.710 --> 20:13.503
You can't stand people like that.

20:14.004 --> 20:14.880
Isn't that right?

20:17.466 --> 20:18.592
I can't say anything.

20:19.426 --> 20:23.138
Mm, because, no matter which path
you chose, Igarashi would've gotten hurt

20:23.222 --> 20:24.389
either way, right?

20:24.473 --> 20:27.267
So, really, I don't think that's
your fault, is it?

20:27.809 --> 20:31.146
And also, I couldn't possibly start
hating you out of the blue after

20:31.230 --> 20:32.606
all these years of friendship

20:32.689 --> 20:35.150
Besides, that's a dumb reason to hate
someone.

20:35.234 --> 20:36.526
BASHFUL...

20:36.610 --> 20:38.528
Uh! All right!

20:38.612 --> 20:41.490
Let's erase the past by having
awesome love lives now!

20:41.990 --> 20:44.076
What? That's okay, I don't really...

20:44.159 --> 20:47.663
- You can go date for both of us.
- I wonder what kind of guy he'll be.

20:47.746 --> 20:48.956
Huh?

20:49.873 --> 20:51.041
- Hmm.
- Okay, let's see.

20:51.750 --> 20:54.670
Obviously you should be with
someone who's the complete opposite of

20:54.753 --> 20:55.587
Igarashi.

20:55.671 --> 20:58.799
Someone who's kind but maybe
scatterbrained in a cute way.

20:58.882 --> 21:02.719
You should be with someone who embraces
everything you are, the way you are.

21:02.803 --> 21:05.764
Someone who's extremely accepting and
kind to other people.

21:07.641 --> 21:08.475
Hold on, this is about you, not me.

21:08.558 --> 21:09.393
WE SYNCHRONIZED...

21:09.476 --> 21:11.770
Hold on, this is about you, not me.

21:14.731 --> 21:17.901
Well, romantic relationships aren't
everything, right?

21:17.985 --> 21:21.947
And I'm having fun right now, but if we
had boyfriends, it would add more color

21:22.030 --> 21:23.198
to our lives!

21:23.949 --> 21:25.617
Like the tomatoes in a bento box.

21:27.411 --> 21:28.996
What kind of metaphor is that?

21:29.079 --> 21:30.080
Yeah, I dunno.

21:31.415 --> 21:32.249
Romance...

21:32.791 --> 21:35.502
Tell me the truth Koyuki, are you
really into Igarashi?

21:35.585 --> 21:36.753
ATAGAWA

21:38.255 --> 21:39.214
It's not like that.

21:39.923 --> 21:41.800
They're all just repeating the rumor.

21:42.634 --> 21:43.468
What?

21:45.971 --> 21:46.805
So you know...

21:46.888 --> 21:49.474
Atagawa's been coming on to me
super strong lately.

21:51.435 --> 21:54.146
Although, I'm not into in anyone but
the girl I like.

21:54.688 --> 21:56.398
She's barking up the wrong tree.

22:04.448 --> 22:05.282
You know, Miki...

22:06.533 --> 22:09.536
The harsh truth is I just don't have
a pure heart like you do.

22:09.619 --> 22:10.579
See ya!

22:10.662 --> 22:12.289
I'll be waiting for your tomato report!

22:12.372 --> 22:14.791
- If I'm honest, I really don't think...
- Ha! "Tomato report"!

22:14.875 --> 22:16.585
I should inflict myself on anyone.

22:18.253 --> 22:19.087
And so...

22:22.841 --> 22:24.634
I hope you go find happiness, Miki.
